# Environment Configuration

This file lists all configuration variables used by VocabVault.
Copy this file to `.env` and fill in values appropriate for your environment.

```env
# ===========================================
# VocabVault — Environment Variables
# ===========================================

# App Configuration
# ---------------
# The display name of the application shown in the browser tab.
VITE_APP_TITLE=VocabVault

# Set to "production" when building for deployment.
# Controls logging verbosity and dev-only features.
VITE_APP_ENV=development

# API Configuration
# ---------------
# Base URL for the backend API.
# Currently the app runs entirely client-side with LocalStorage,
# but this variable is reserved for future API integration.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Feature Flags
# ---------------
# Enable or disable optional features at runtime.
# Set to "true" to enable, "false" to disable.

# Enable import/export functionality (default: true)
VITE_FEATURE_IMPORT_EXPORT=true

# Enable progress tracking and dashboard statistics (default: true)
VITE_FEATURE_PROGRESS_TRACKING=true

# Enable spaced repetition review mode (default: true)
VITE_FEATURE_SRS_REVIEW=true

# Enable search and filter in the flashcard browser (default: true)
VITE_FEATURE_SEARCH_FILTER=true

# SRS Algorithm Tuning
# ---------------
# Override default spaced repetition parameters.
# Leave blank to use built-in defaults.

# Initial interval (in days) for new cards
VITE_SRS_INITIAL_INTERVAL=

# Minimum ease factor (prevents intervals from collapsing)
VITE_SRS_MINIMUM_EASE_FACTOR=

# Logging
# ---------------
# Set the minimum log level: debug, info, warn, error
VITE_LOG_LEVEL=info
```

---

## Notes

- All variables are prefixed with `VITE_` so they are exposed to the client via `import.meta.env`.
- Variables without a `VITE_` prefix are **never** exposed to the browser.
- The app is fully functional without any environment variables set.
- After editing this file, restart the dev server for changes to take effect.
